    "body": "## Description\n\n`geometry3k_reward_fn` in `areal/reward/geometry3k.py` ran `extract_answer` on the gold answer with its last-number fallback on. About one in ten Geometry3K answers are LaTeX (in the first 100 test rows: `5 \\sqrt { 3 }`, `4 \\frac { 4 } { 11 }`, `\\sqrt { 21 }`, `6 \\sqrt { 6 }`, ...), so the gold answer became its last number (`3`, `11`, `21`). Passing the bare LaTeX to math-verify had the same effect, because its expression extractor also picks the last number.\n\nBefore (gold `5 \\sqrt { 3 }`):\n- `The answer is [5\\sqrt{3}].` -> 0.0\n- `The answer is [3].` -> 1.0\n\nAfter:\n- `The answer is [5\\sqrt{3}].` -> 1.0\n- `The answer is [3].` -> 0.0\n\nNumeric gold answers (`48`, `7.85`) score the same as before.\n\nThis PR:\n- takes only a bracketed value from the gold answer (`use_last_number=False`) and otherwise keeps the raw string;\n- wraps both sides in `$...$` before `MathVerifyWorker.verify` so they are parsed as one LaTeX expression;\n- adds `test_geometry3k_latex_ground_truth` to `tests/test_math_verify_reward.py`.\n\nNote: `examples/vlm/geometry3k_grpo.py` scores with the `\\boxed{}` reward in `areal/workflow/openai/geometry3k_agent.py`, so the example itself is not affected; this fixes the public `areal.reward.geometry3k_reward_fn`.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNone found (searched open and closed issues and PRs).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the\n  [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`). I ran ruff (v0.14.9) lint and format on the changed files only.\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):**\n\nN/A\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe new test fails on current `main` and passes with this change; all 70 tests in `tests/test_math_verify_reward.py` pass (CPU only).\n\nAI use: I used an AI coding assistant (Claude Code) while writing the fix and tests; I reviewed the changes and ran the checks listed above.\n",
